---
import LearningLayout from "../layouts/LearningLayout.astro";
import ScanCycleIsland from "../components/ScanCycleIsland.astro";
---

<LearningLayout
  title="Salbotics PLC Learning Hub - How It Works"
  eyebrow="Migrated guide page spike"
>
  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <div>
        <h1>How the PLC scan-cycle lesson works.</h1>
        <p>
          This is the first migrated guide-page spike. It proves Astro can share
          layout, navigation, footer, and interactive SVG teaching components
          before the full static page set is migrated.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ScanCycleIsland />
    </section>

    <section class="panel">
      <h2>Guide structure preserved</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Inputs</h3>
          <p>Students read start, stop, pedestrian, vehicle, emergency, and night-mode inputs before logic is solved.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Logic</h3>
          <p>The local Python engine remains the source of truth for the scan cycle, timers, registers, and alarms.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Outputs</h3>
          <p>The HMI shows red, yellow, green, all-red gaps, alarms, event history, and rung-monitor status.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</LearningLayout>
